# C3: the std submodules mlmf-source-file may name.
#
# **This is a source-axis crate and the allow-list is NOT relaxed for it.**
# C3's scope — "no crate on the format axis references `std::fs`, `memmap2`,
# or any network client" — is what `tests/axis` releases, and it releases
# exactly one name, `memmap2`, in the two gates that check crate names. The
# `std` half is per-crate and unchanged on both axes: `purity.rs` checks
# every `std::X` this crate's `src/**` reaches against this file, whatever
# axis it declares. Reading `std::fs` here therefore costs an entry below,
# exactly as `iter` costs mlmf-safetensors one.
#
# Grows one commit at a time, each entry landing beside the code that forced
# it and saying what that was. A permission granted before its use is a
# permission nobody re-examines.
#
# `purity.rs` scans `src/**` INCLUDING `#[cfg(test)]` modules and does not
# scan `tests/`. This crate keeps its tests in `tests/`, so this file records
# only what the library reaches — `tests/bytes.rs` uses `std::fs` and
# `env!("CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR")` freely and neither appears here.

# Task 1, the plain-read path. Each entry names what forced it.
#
# `fmt` -- `impl std::fmt::Debug for FileSource`, hand-written because a
#   derived one formats every byte of the file. There is no spelling of a
#   `Debug` impl that does not name `std::fmt`. The plan predicted `fs` and
#   `path` alone for this task; the impl was forced by `Result::expect_err`,
#   which requires `T: Debug`, in this crate's own first test. Recorded as a
#   divergence rather than folded in silently.
# `fs` -- `std::fs::read` in `FileSource::open_read`. This is the crate's
#   entire purpose: the source axis is I/O, and the format axis is where
#   C3's prohibition on reaching the filesystem belongs.
# `path` -- `open`/`open_read` take `&std::path::Path`, which is the type
#   `mlmf_core::Error::with_path` already accepts and the type a consumer
#   already holds.
#
# Task 2, `RangedSource`. One entry, and it is not optional:
#
# `ops` -- `RangedSource::read_range(&self, range: Range<u64>, ...)` is
#   declared with `std::ops::Range` in `mlmf-core`'s `traits.rs`, which
#   writes `use std::ops::Range;` at its own line 8 for the same reason.
#   An implementation of that method cannot spell its own signature
#   without naming the type, so this entry is forced by the seam rather
#   than chosen by this crate. `PathBuf` came with it and cost nothing:
#   `path` was already listed above.
#
# `io` is NOT here and its absence is load-bearing rather than incidental:
#   `std::fs::read` returns `std::io::Result`, and the error conversion
#   reaches that type without naming it only because the `map_err` closure
#   argument is left unannotated. Spelling it `|e: std::io::Error|` is an
#   ordinary readability edit and the gate reports it -- measured, in both
#   directions. `src/file.rs` carries that note where the edit would be
#   typed.
fmt
fs
ops
path
